; Literal characters loaded (#1018, spec editor/literal-characters): a
; tokenised file with the pairs $90 DF, $90 E9 in a string and $90 E9 in a
; comment, loaded under blitz2 (ted_ab_originals: with the userlib
; literallib.obj, which names the words), SAVE over it, QUIT.  The saved
; file equals the loaded one in every combination (@roundtrip).  The
; original TED shows the names in the token colour, with glyphs from behind
; its font (it has none from 128); TED-C draws glyph 0 in the colour of the
; text: the screens of the original and TED-C differ.
; @file lit.bb2 "a$=\"Gr\x1b\x90\xdfe \x90\xe9\"\x00\xdd\x82 a$\x00; caf\x90\xe9\x00"
; @source F lit.bb2
; @roundtrip
; @fixed #1018 R5-C5 Rc-Cc
; @est 3
timeout 10
wait req "OKEE DOKEE"
gad 1
wait screen
dump start
menu 0 2
wait freq "Name to save file as"
freq ok
wait screen
dump saved
menu 0 9
wait exit
